"Governed mutation evidence replay"},"claim_ceiling":"validates declared public contract only","claim_ceiling_restated":"Checks synthetic mutation proposals against their proof cells, policy verdicts, evidence-chain hash, rollback records and a Git commit, and rejects a proposal with a single verdict, a stale hash or a missing rollback.","claim_id":"claim::proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization","evidence_class":"semantic_validator","evidence_strength_rank":5,"organ_id":"proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation","validator_command":"python -m microcosm_core.organs.proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization run --input fixtures/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/input --out receipts/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization"},"claim_clause_coverage":{"claim_text_sha256":"803dee36585b3b5457034bc188b5bc133ebd31a8c658eb87dca5a73e530cd5ce","clauses":[],"mapped_clause_count":null,"status":"unknown","whole_claim_coverage":"unknown"},"classification":{"evidence_class":"semantic_validator","family":"formal_math_and_proof","real_substrate_disposition":"real_substrate_capsule","truth_accounting_bucket":"real_import_validation"},"component_id":"proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization","evidence_state":{"current_backend_binding":{"status":"not_checked"},"fresh_prover":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"fresh_replay":{"status":"not_recorded_by_index"},"index_state":"retained_generated_snapshot"},"guide":{"availability":"available","guide_id":"paper_module.proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization","plain":"A system that changes things automatically needs evidence that each change was checked, allowed by policy and can be undone. This component is given made-up change proposals, each linked to proof records, policy rulings, an undo record and a version-control record. It looks up each record, recalculates a fingerprint summarizing the evidence, checks the version-control record, and rejects a proposal with only one visible policy ruling, a stale fingerprint or no undo record for a reversible write. It writes a saved record of whether each proposal's evidence holds together, showing which are properly backed.","plain_availability":"available","ref":"paper_modules/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization.md","sha256":"09886dc61981d2ff62000af668b5f6b9d1c972dcbca4bc57496b888da6125890","text":"# Governed mutation evidence replay\n\n> **In plain terms.** A system that changes things automatically needs evidence that each change was checked, allowed by policy and can be undone. This component is given made-up change proposals, each linked to proof records, policy rulings, an undo record and a version-control record. It looks up each record, recalculates a fingerprint summarizing the evidence, checks the version-control record, and rejects a proposal with only one visible policy ruling, a stale fingerprint or no undo record for a reversible write. It writes a saved record of whether each proposal's evidence holds together, showing which are properly backed.\n\nChecks synthetic mutation proposals against linked proof, policy, side-effect, rollback and replay records, then writes an authorization replay receipt.\n\n## Run the example\n\nFrom the repository root with Python 3.11 or newer:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization run --input fixtures/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/input --out .microcosm/component-guides/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization --acceptance-out .microcosm/component-guides/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/acceptance.json --card\n```\n\nInspect the status and findings in `.microcosm/component-guides/`; the linked result below is a historical sample.\n\n## What it checks\n\nFor each proposal, the validator resolves proof cells and visible policy verdicts, recomputes an evidence-chain hash and checks the associated record. Write and rollback proposals require side-effect and rollback records. It also checks a Git commit witness and its changed paths; Git must be installed and the referenced commit available. A proposal with one visible verdict, a stale hash or no rollback for a reversible write is rejected.\n\n## Limits\n\nChecks synthetic mutation proposals against their proof cells, policy verdicts, evidence-chain hash, rollback records and a Git commit, and rejects a proposal with a single verdict, a stale hash or a missing rollback.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe focused tests exercise this component’s checks; they do not prove its algorithm. `make component-replays` runs its registered exported authorization bundle through the shared [Dafny admission check](../formal/replay/README.md), which checks source, input, claim-policy and receipt agreement within the host’s observations. The direct command above does not itself invoke that admission gate.\n\n## Source and evidence\n\n- [Implementation](../src/microcosm_core/organs/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization.py) and [focused tests](../tests/test_proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization.py)\n- [Example input](../fixtures/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/input/mutation_proposals.json) and [historical sample result](../receipts/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization_result.json)\n- [Component JSON record](./proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization.json) and [canonical capsule](../core/paper_module_capsules.json)\n\nFor policy-engine context see [Open Policy Agent](https://www.openpolicyagent.org/docs), [Kubernetes admission controllers](https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/admission-controllers/), and [feature toggles](https://martinfowler.com/articles/feature-toggles.html).\n"},"proofs":[],"replay":{"command":"make component-replays","command_ref":"scripts/check/check_component_replays.py","command_scope":"all registered components","configuration_refs":["src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#RUNTIME_STEPS","src/microcosm_core/runtime_shell.py#_accepted_organ_runner_module_refs"],"declared_prerequisites":{"availability_status":"not_assessed_by_index","description":"Lean, Swift and test extras required","source_ref":"Makefile"},"execution_status":"not_run_by_index","fresh_receipt_template":".microcosm/component-replays/<run>/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/exported_governed_mutation_authorization_bundle_validation_result.json","guide_example":{"command":"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m microcosm_core.organs.proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization run --input fixtures/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/input --out receipts/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization --acceptance-out receipts/acceptance/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization_fixture_acceptance.json","expected_result_description":{"status":"unrecorded"},"prerequisites_description":{"see":"paper_modules/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization.md","status":"unrecorded"},"scope":"verbatim historical Atlas example; not an execution request and may target retained receipt paths","source_field":"organs[proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization].first_command","source_ref":"core/organ_atlas.json","usage":"verbatim_source_example_only","writes_retained_receipts":true},"input_mode":"exported_governed_mutation_authorization_bundle","input_ref":"examples/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization/exported_governed_mutation_authorization_bundle","last_result":{"artifact_ref":"receipts/acceptance/first_wave/proof_derived_governed_mutation_authorization_fixture_acceptance.json","artifact_sha256":"9ae972aaf931deb5d54b085c31fe9f0e6b9cca5ec8571bac38ce7cb6d97e24da","availability":"available","created_at":"2026-05-27T02:53:57+00:00","freshness":"historical_saved_artifact","input_mode":null,"native_observations":{"execution_witness